  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-10-12T16:34:25.870Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Related to \"Decoupled Headlook (like Onward) (Hand-Directed Movement)\" but I'm unsure if it's impeded by the same thing.\nI started using a hip tracker recently (old Vive wand) and the first thing I noticed was how weird it is that my avatar always moves where I'm looking rather than where I'm turned, making it impossible for me to look around while walking. When a hip tracker is present, I imagine VRChat should have the data it needs for real forward movement. Could this be added as an option?",
